From 6a93795d45cc435ae8d69f4ca976fdbdffc92607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:52:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): soft deadline + kanban_continue checkpoint
 instead of dying at max_runtime [daveey]

At kanban.soft_deadline_fraction (0.85) of max_runtime_seconds the worker gets an
OUT-OF-BAND steer (and a final one near the cap) to checkpoint with the new
kanban_continue tool. The run closes as outcome 'continued' and the card is
re-queued at once (or after resume_after_seconds, woken by the dispatcher tick),
with the checkpoint rendered at the top of the next run's context ahead of the
b78e9861e6 transcript tail. Continuations never touch consecutive_failures or
block_recurrences; their own bound is kanban.max_continuations (12). The hard
kill at 100% is unchanged. Kanban workers starting a background job are told to
hand long waits off with resume_after_seconds instead of polling (14-day data:
61% of timed-out run time was sleep/poll on CI, releases and soaks).
